# The Hemp Press's part sheets.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw these; that is what the .mctex is for. The geometry that
# maps them lives in textures-src/hemp_press.bbmodel (open it in Blockbench) -- every face there has an
# explicit UV into one of these sheets, so a redraw keeps to the rectangles below.
#
# A screw press on a hemp-brick bed: the frame and the bed are block/hemp_bricks_block unchanged, the
# crossbeam is oak bound in iron, and the moving part is an iron platen driven down a threaded rod by
# a four-spoke capstan with twine-wrapped grips. Iron tones are the ones the old flat press faces used
# (sampled from vanilla's block/iron_block). The oak is vanilla's block/piston_top ramp, so the piston
# the recipe puts in the middle is the timber you see -- and brown, where the bricks are olive.
#
# Layouts, in pixels (x y w h):
#   hemp_press_iron       platen top 0 0 10 10 | platen side 0 10 10 2 | hub top 10 0 4 4
#                         hub side 10 4 4 2 | rod side 14 0 2 4 | spoke 0 12 10 1, underside 0 13 10 1,
#                         spoke end 10 12 1 1
#   hemp_press_plate(_hot) plate top 0 0 12 12 | plate side 0 12 12 1 | vent 0 13 6 2 | vent top 0 15 6 1
#   hemp_press_beam       front 0 0 16 3 | top and underside 0 3 16 6 | end grain 0 9 6 3
#   hemp_press_parchment  top 0 0 6 6 | side 0 6 6 1

@palette default
. = none
1 = 2E2A27      iron, the bore
2 = 4B4642      iron, seams and shadow
3 = 6E6862      iron, unlit face
4 = 8A837C      iron, body
5 = A69E96      iron, lit face
6 = C4BCB2      iron, polished
t = A1976C      twine
T = C9BC8C      twine, lit
u = 6E6644      twine, shadow
w = 67502C      beam oak, seam
x = 7E6237      beam oak, dark
y = 9F844D      beam oak, mid
z = AF8F55      beam oak, light
Z = C29D62      beam oak, lit
a = 5A544E      cold ash
g = 3E3935      cold ash, deep
r = 5A1E14      hot iron, shadowed edge
R = 8A2E12      hot iron, dull red
m = A8380E      hot iron, red -- the body of the plate
o = CA4E06      glowing
O = E8701A      glowing, bright
Y = F8A040      the hottest, straight over the fire -- a few pixels only
p = E3D5A8      parchment
P = CDBB88      parchment, fold
q = B09D6C      parchment, shadow
j = E4AE45      rosin, lit
k = C98A1E      rosin
K = 9A5E12      rosin, pooled

