# The same plate over a fire, and it glows. Same layout, so the model only swaps the texture. The
# whole plate goes red -- a hashish press really runs at 80-100 C and would never glow, but this is
# a readability call, made by Warlon Mhite after three subtler drafts: the heat has to read at a
# glance, and only a red plate does. The heat gathers in an irregular patch over the middle, where
# the fire is, with a few yellow-hot pixels at its heart; never a symmetric diamond, which is what
# made the very first draft look like a sprite stamped on. Bolts and grate glow with it.
@texture block/hemp_press_plate_hot 16x16 type=block
RmmmmmmmmmmRRRRR
mOmmmmmmmmOrRRRR
mmmmommmmmmrRRRR
mmmoOOommmmrRRRR
mmoOYOOoommrRRRR
mmoOYYOOOomrRRRR
mmmoOYYOoomrRRRR
mmmoOOOoommrRRRR
mmmmooommmmrRRRR
mmmmmmmommmrRRRR
mOmmmmmmmmOrRRRR
RrrrrrrrrrrrRRRR
RmmmmmmmmmmrRRRR
2Y2O2YRRRRRRRRRR
2O2o2ORRRRRRRRRR
rrrrrrRRRRRRRRRR

